  "reactionVersion": 1,
  "mechanismSummary": "Toluenesulfonic acid protonates dihydropyran on carbon; the ring oxygen stabilises the cation as an oxocarbenium ion. Cyclohexanol adds to it, and tosylate takes the proton back. The tetrahydropyranyl (THP) ether is an acetal: it survives strong base, Grignard reagents and LiAlH₄, and comes off with aqueous acid (or TsOH in methanol) by the reverse mechanism. A new stereogenic centre forms at the acetal carbon, so chiral alcohols give diastereomers. Pyridinium tosylate (PPTS) is a milder acid for the same job. The app does not check stereochemistry yet.",
